From: razgulay <bantran09@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:10:28 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(cors):=20answer=20browser=20preflights=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20add=20CORS=20middleware=20for=20/v1/*?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The gateway emitted no CORS headers at all and chi's route tree answered
preflight OPTIONS /v1/messages with 405 (Allow: POST), so every
browser-based client (Claude for Office webview, web apps) died at
preflight with a bare "Failed to fetch". curl/SDK clients never noticed
because they do not enforce CORS.

internal/middleware.CORS, mounted right after RequestID in
internal/app.ProvideRouter:
- preflight (OPTIONS + Origin) answered 204 before routing, so it can
  never fall through to chi's 405; allow-headers echo the browser's
  Access-Control-Request-Headers when present, else the known set
  (x-api-key, authorization, content-type, anthropic-version,
  anthropic-beta); Access-Control-Max-Age=86400 caches it.
- real requests carrying an Origin get Access-Control-Allow-Origin
  reflected (not "*", so credentialed requests stay possible) plus
  Vary: Origin.
- no Origin (curl, SDKs) — untouched.

Auth is per-request x-api-key, not cookies, so no
Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: an origin needs the header value to
get anywhere, and reflecting its own Origin grants nothing extra.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
